{"step_index":126,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:00:26Z","input_tokens":2519,"cache_read_tokens":137393,"output_tokens":927,"thinking":"The assertion failure arises from differing rounding methods. Python 3's `round()` function employs \"round half to even\" (banker's rounding), leading `round(52.5)` to evaluate to 52. PostgreSQL's `ROUND()` function, along with standard arithmetic, utilizes \"half-up\" rounding, resulting in `ROUND(52.5)` evaluating to 53. This difference explains the unexpected assertion.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\ashmi\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\civicsync\\\\tests\\\\test_civicsync_core.py\"","Replacement":"\"def calculate_priority_score(\\n    hazard_class: str,\\n    extent: str,\\n    confidence: float,\\n    location_context: float,\\n    reporter_count: int\\n) -> (int, str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Deterministic Priority Scoring Formula (RULES.pdf §1.1) matching SQL ROUND()\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    c = CLASSES[hazard_class]\\n    e = EXTENTS[extent]\\n    k = max(0.0, min(1.0, confidence))\\n    l = location_context\\n    b = min(10, 3 * max(0, reporter_count - 1))\\n\\n    # Standard half-up rounding matching PostgreSQL ROUND()\\n    inner = 100.0 * (0.30 * c + 0.25 * e + 0.15 * k + 0.30 * l)\\n    raw = math.floor(inner + 0.5) + b\\n    score = min(100, max(0, raw))\\n\\n    if score >= 75:\\n        band = \\\"critical\\\"\\n    elif score >= 55:\\n        band = \\\"high\\\"\\n    elif score >= 35:\\n        band = \\\"medium\\\"\\n    else:\\n        band = \\\"low\\\"\\n\\n    return score, band\"","Target":"\"def calculate_priority_score(\\n    hazard_class: str,\\n    extent: str,\\n    confidence: float,\\n    location_context: float,\\n    reporter_count: int\\n) -> (int, str):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Deterministic Priority Scoring Formula (RULES.pdf §1.1)\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    c = CLASSES[hazard_class]\\n    e = EXTENTS[extent]\\n    k = max(0.0, min(1.0, confidence))\\n    l = location_context\\n    b = min(10, 3 * max(0, reporter_count - 1))\\n\\n    raw = round(100.0 * (0.30 * c + 0.25 * e + 0.15 * k + 0.30 * l)) + b\\n    score = min(100, max(0, raw))\\n\\n    if score >= 75:\\n        band = \\\"critical\\\"\\n    elif score >= 55:\\n        band = \\\"high\\\"\\n    elif score >= 35:\\n        band = \\\"medium\\\"\\n    else:\\n        band = \\\"low\\\"\\n\\n    return score, band\""}}]}
