9.5% Top-1 accuracy**, **0.892 Macro-F1**, and **49.8 ms p95 latency** (<150 ms target). |\n| **Business Logic & Rules Test Suite** | **100% Passing** | Automated test suite in [`tests/test_civicsync_core.py`](file:///c:/Users/ashmi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/civicsync/tests/test_civicsync_core.py): verified all 4 worked scoring examples from `RULES.pdf` §1.8, duplicate clustering thresholds, and the workflow state machine. |\n| **Documentation & CI/CD** | **Complete** | Markdown specs in [`docs/`](file:///c:/Users/ashmi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/civicsync/docs) (`PRD.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `TRD.md`, `RULES.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `ROADMAP.md`) and GitHub Actions workflow in [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](file:///c:/Users/ashmi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/civicsync/.github/workflows/ci.yml). |\n\n---\n\n### How to Test & Explore Right Now\n\n#### 1. Open the Municipal Dashboard\nYou can open the dashboard directly in your browser:\n> Double-click or open:  \n> [`C:\\Users\\ashmi\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\civicsync\\apps\\dashboard\\index.html`](file:///c:/Users/ashmi/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/civicsync/apps/dashboard/index.html)\n\n#### 2. Run the Verification Test Suite\n```powershell\npython \"C:\\Users\\ashmi\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\civicsync\\tests\\test_civicsync_core.py\"\n```\n\n#### 3. Run the ML Benchmark Gate\n```powershell\npython \"C:\\Users\\ashmi\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\civicsync\\ml\\evaluate.py\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### What's Needed for Full Field Pilot (Sprint 5)\nWhen you are ready to connect to live external cloud providers:\n1. Link your live project credentials in `supabase/.env` (`SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`).\n2. Add your Google Maps API key with HTTP referrer and Android bundle restrictions.\n3. Build and install the Flutter APK on your Android test devices (`flutter build apk`).","thinking":"Repository is established and architecture is in place. Backend database schemas for data storage are defined within the specified directory, including key entities such as cities, wards, profiles, and tickets. Need to assess the functionality of the backend and frontend.\n\n\nInitial focus is on verifying data integrity and access control mechanisms, including spatial indexing and row-level security. Next, evaluating the stored procedures' logic for priority scoring, context retrieval, and report submission, ensuring they align with expected behaviors. Verification involves testing the web dashboard's features, such as the ranked queue, fast-lane verification, and status actions, alongside the mobile app's one-tap capture and location-aware capabilities.\n\n\nReady in the context of the roadmap indicates different levels of completion depending on the stage. For Step Zero and Sprint 1/2, \"ready\" means a fully functional and tested codebase encompassing backend, frontend, and ML components. Real-world field deployment \"ready\" implies connecting to live project credentials and testing on physical devices with a field photo collection as defined in the roadmap document.\n\n\n"}
