{"step_index":145,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:28:12Z","input_tokens":148545,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":359,"thinking":"The existing single-page layout for the Municipal Dashboard frontend needs significant improvement. The goal is to enhance its visual appeal and professional appearance, while still retaining all features on a single page, meaning a refactoring of the current structure is required. The current rudimentary aesthetic needs to be elevated.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"100","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\ashmi\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\builtin\\\\skills\\\\generative_ui\\\\SKILL.md\"","StartLine":"1"}}]}
{"step_index":146,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:28:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T20:58:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T20:58:39+05:30\nShowing lines 1-100 of 123\n1: ---\n2: name: generative_ui\n3: description: How to render rich interactive HTML widgets inline in the chat or as standalone artifacts. Use this skill when you want to show the user diagrams, data visualizations, interactive controls, educational walkthroughs, or any rich visual content beyond plain text and markdown.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Generative UI\n7: \n8: You can render custom, rich, interactive user interfaces (inline widgets or\n9: larger artifacts) directly in the chat. This is a great way to communicate\n10: complex information to the user, generate rich visualizations, and even create\n11: small interactive experiences for the user.\n12: \n13: ## Workflow\n14: \n15: 1.  **Create the HTML Artifact**: Use `write_to_file` to save a self-contained\n16:     `.html` file (using Tailwind CSS and inline JavaScript) to the artifact\n17:     directory. Set `UserFacing: true` in `ArtifactMetadata`.\n18: 2.  **Embed Inline (optional)**: Include the `<agent-embed>` tag in your chat\n19:     response, if you decide this html artifact should be rendered inline in the\n20:     conversation:\n21: \n22:     ```\n23:     <agent-embed src=\"file:///<artifact_path>/widget.html\"></agent-embed>\n24:     ```\n25: \n26: ## Constraints & Theming\n27: \n28: *   **External Assets & Tailwind CSS**: All external CDNs are blocked by CSP,\n29:     except for one allowlisted gstatic Tailwind dependency that you **CAN** and\n30:     **SHOULD** use to style your artifacts. Include the following script tag in\n31:     your `<head>` to enable Tailwind:\n32: \n33:     ```html\n34:     <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\"></script>\n35:     ```\n36: \n37: *   **Use Provided Theme Variables**: The iframe injects the app's semantic\n38:     design-system tokens, so widgets automatically match the host theme and the\n39:     user's custom colors. Surfaces (`--background`, `--content`, `--card`,\n40:     `--sidebar`), borders (`--border`), \n<truncated 1094 bytes>\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n61:     <html>\n62:     <head>\n63:       <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/antigravity/web/dev/tailwindcss.min.js\"></script>\n64:     </head>\n65:     <body class=\"bg-transparent text-[var(--foreground)] antialiased p-5\">\n66:       <div class=\"bg-[var(--card)] text-[var(--foreground)] border border-[var(--border)] rounded-xl p-5 shadow-sm\">\n67:         <h2 class=\"text-[var(--foreground)] font-semibold text-lg\">Title</h2>\n68:         <p class=\"text-[var(--muted-foreground)] text-sm\">Description</p>\n69:         <!-- Interactive content goes here -->\n70:       </div>\n71:     </body>\n72:     </html>\n73:     ```\n74: \n75: *   **General styling**: Aim for a clean, premium aesthetic. For `<canvas>`,\n76:     check `document.documentElement.classList.contains('light')` to adapt\n77:     colors.\n78: \n79: ## Deciding on Placement (Inline vs. Standalone)\n80: \n81: **Default to artifact only** — reference the HTML artifact in your response and\n82: let the user open it in the side pane. Consider inlining when the widget is\n83: compact (comfortably under 500px tall) and directly illustrates the surrounding\n84: explanation (e.g., a small educational widget, plot, or diagram). Larger, more\n85: complex content (data dashboards, simulations, app prototypes) should stay\n86: artifact-only. Always follow the user's explicit preference if stated.\n87: \n88: ## Designing Inline Widgets (Cards & Transparency)\n89: \n90: When embedding inline in chat (`<agent-embed>`), style widgets as native chat\n91: components:\n92: \n93: *   **Transparent Root Background**: Always set `<body class=\"bg-transparent\n94:     ...\">` so the widget blends seamlessly into the chat container.\n95: *   **Card-Based Layouts**: Wrap inline content and controls in a card container\n96:     (as shown in the Boilerplate Template above) to provide elevation and\n97:     prevent loose text in light mode.\n98: *   **Standalone Artifacts**: For full-page side-pane artifacts (like\n99:     dashboards), use a solid background (e.g., `bg-[var(--background)]`).\n100: ","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":147,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:28:39Z","input_tokens":3133,"cache_read_tokens":147363,"output_tokens":21963,"thinking":"Initial assessment: The frontend needs visual enhancement to convey a professional appearance, moving beyond a basic design. This implies a need for a modern, polished aesthetic suitable for a professional setting, such as an enterprise SaaS or command-center interface. Design decisions will prioritize clear, crisp typography and subtle visual effects.\n\n\nThe initial design direction emphasizes a visual language consistent with enterprise-grade applications. Key UI elements will include sleek interactions, accessible high-contrast colors, polished stat cards, and visual effects like glassmorphism. This approach aims for an intuitive, professional feel.\n\nThe monolithic single-page design needs to evolve into a multi-view application. Dedicated views will be created for triage, geospatial analysis, duplicate resolution, SLA monitoring, and analytics, each providing focused functionality. This enhances usability and information accessibility.\n\n\nThe initial step is to create a fully functional, browser-compatible dashboard.  An interactive artifact will be generated, allowing direct user interaction within the environment. I'll define the application's structure, including a header with operational status and navigation tabs for various views.\n\n\nNow designing the main triage view with high-fidelity ticket cards incorporating dynamic score badges, hazard indicators, and SLA progress.  Focusing on a clear visual hierarchy to quickly convey critical information and enable rapid action through direct buttons or a slide-over drawer for detailed information. The drawer will include detailed ticket information, photo comparisons, interactive maps, and a citizen corroboration timeline to enhance the decision-making process.\n\nConsidering implementing a second view using a GIS density map centered on relevant locations to provide spatial context. This map will use density grid polygons and cluster markers to visualize ticket concentrations and identify areas of high impact for resource allocation. This will provide actionable insights for field crew dispatch.\n\n\nAdding a geospatial view, the design will integrate controls for toggling map layers like wards and density grids, with a summary card showing hazards within the viewport. Developing a split-screen view to resolve duplicate hazards by comparing photos and showing the impact of merging tickets, and offer one-click actions.\n\nAn SLA escalation monitor will provide real-time countdowns against municipal working hours, with tiered alerts based on elapsed time and instant escalation for reopened tickets. A dedicated analytics view will integrate HTML5 charts visualizing hazard class breakdown, inflow/resolution velocity, and turnaround time, along with a CSV export option.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n  <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n  <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n  <title>CivicSync · Municipal Operations Command Center</title>\\n  <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css\\\" />\\n  <script src=\\\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js\\\"></script>\\n  <script src=\\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js\\\"></script>\\n  <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\">\\n  <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\" crossorigin>\\n  <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;600&display=swap\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n\\n  <style>\\n    :root {\\n      --primary: #2563EB;\\n      --primary-dark: #1D4ED8;\\n      --primary-light: #EFF6FF;\\n      --primary-border: #BFDBFE;\\n      --slate-50: #F8FAFC;\\n      --slate-100: #F1F5F9;\\n      --slate-200: #E2E8F0;\\n      --slate-300: #CBD5E1;\\n      --slate-400: #94A3B8;\\n      --slate-500: #64748B;\\n      --slate-600: #475569;\\n      --slate-700: #334155;\\n      --slate-800: #1E293B;\\n      --slate-900: #0F172A;\\n\\n      --critical: #DC2626;\\n      --critical-bg: #FEF2F2;\\n      --critical-border: #FECACA;\\n      --high: #EA580C;\\n      --high-bg: #FFF7ED;\\n      --high-border: #FFEDD5;\\n      --medium: #D97706;\\n      --medium-bg: #FFFBEB;\\n      --medium-border: #FEF3C7;\\n      --low: #16A34A;\\n      --low-bg: #F0FDF4;\\n      --low-border: #DCFCE7;\\n\\n      --radius-sm: 6px;\\n      --radius-md: 10px;\\n      --radius-lg: 14px;\\n      --radius-full: 9999px;\\n      --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\\n      --shadow-md: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08), 0 2px 4px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\\n      --shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 4px 6px -4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\\n      --shadow-xl: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);\\n    }\\n\\n    * { box-sizing:\n<truncated 63811 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\ashmi\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\civicsync\\\\apps\\\\dashboard\\\\index.html\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
